# Cloudflare Pages _headers — security hardening for dev.uyammadu.com
# Place this file at the project root so `npm run build` copies it into dist/.
# Cloudflare Pages reads _headers from the build output root.
#
# Fixes audit findings F-1 (CSP), F-2 (clickjacking), F-3 (HSTS), F-4 (MIME sniffing).
#
# NOTE on CSP: the portfolio uses some inline styles ('unsafe-inline' in style-src)
# and Google Fonts (fonts.googleapis.com stylesheet + fonts.gstatic.com font files),
# which are explicitly allowed below. There is NO inline script relaxation —
# index.js is the only script and is loaded same-origin ('self').
# ROLLOUT STATE: the CSP below is currently in REPORT-ONLY mode — it logs violations
# to the browser console but does NOT block anything, so it cannot break the live site.
# After confirming no legitimate resource is reported as blocked, rename the header from
# `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only` to `Content-Security-Policy` to enforce it.
# All other headers below are enforcing immediately.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Tighten caching/headers for the API route specifically (no caching of dynamic responses)
/api/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
